    "body": "@zcorpan @domenic I'm relatively close to finish, but have one question to discuss. In the updated local version, I described how to consume decimal and hexademical digits as part of the numeric entities through the math conversion rules like in:\n\n``` html\n<dt><span data-x=\"ASCII digits\">ASCII digit</span></dt>\n<dd>Multiply the <var>character reference code</var> by 16. Add numeric version of the\n<span>current input character</span> (subtract 0x0030 from the character's code point) to the\n<var>character reference code</var>.</dd>\n```\n\nBut now I found that spec uses number decoding in other places without such definitions, so wondering if it's too excessive to do so and better to leave that piece intact?\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/html/issues/comments/215112377/reactions",
