    "created_at": "2016-04-27T18:15:47Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-04-27T18:15:47Z",
    "body": "My knee-jerk reaction is that a code point and a \"number\" might be different types which could make it a bit confusing to say to subtract a number from a code point and use the resulting code point as a number. The existing \"interpret the string of characters as a number (either hexadecimal or decimal as appropriate)\", while not providing an algorithm for doing so, still seems clear enough to result in interoperable implementations since the string can only ever contain the right characters.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
