    "created_at": "2016-04-27T18:33:22Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-04-27T18:33:22Z",
    "body": "> Code points are numbers (integers), by definition, so adding or subtracting integers from them to get other code points is completely well-defined and reasonable.\n\nIt basically depends on if you're doing C-style typedefs or ML-style wrapper types. The latter can be useful for clarity and correctness instead of just assuming all things that are \"really\" integers can be operated on together.\n",
